{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1169","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1169","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1169\",\"parent_revision\":\"aa3542fc8e1e1da2806c124bd32f217b9bc9e4da\",\"root_revision\":\"3a5abd8f275331133f9c73685289beda66fd0d614040f8f1bae20bd5b79a69d2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **hallucination-detector: fix dead backtick evidence marker and multi-occurrence 'because' bug** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Plugin code review session 2026-02-21\\n- **Priority**: completed\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Hook correctness issue: false negatives (missed flags) and false positives (wrong suppression) degrade the hallucination-detector's core value proposition. Affects every assistant turn that contains inline code near causal language.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an assistant message contains `because` (or other causal phrases) near backtick-wrapped inline code, the hook should suppress the causality flag \u2014 treating inline code as observable evidence. When `because` appears multiple times in a message, each occurrence is evaluated independently: occurrences with nearby evidence are suppressed, occurrences without are flagged. The hedged-because pattern (`probably because`, `likely because`, etc.) is flagged exactly once per message regardless of occurrence count.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe target state: two bugs confirmed fixed in `scripts/hallucination-audit-stop.cjs` (in the `bitflight-devops/hallucination-detector` repo), with regression tests in `tests/hallucination-audit-stop.test.cjs` covering both scenarios. The test suite passes under `npx vitest run`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `findTriggerMatches('The test fails because \\\\`exit code 127\\\\` was returned by the process.')` returns zero `causality_language` matches \u2014 inline code suppresses the flag via `rawText` path.\\n2. `findTriggerMatches('It failed because \\\\`exit code 1\\\\` was returned. Also because the config is wrong.')` returns exactly 1 `causality_language` match with `evidence === 'because'` \u2014 the suppressed first occurrence is not counted, the unsuppressed second is.\\n3. `findTriggerMatches('This probably fails because the path is wrong. It also probably fails because the env is wrong.')` returns at least 1 match with `evidence === 'because (hedged)'` and no more than 1 (hedged-because is one-flag-per-message by design).\\n4. All existing tests in `tests/hallucination-audit-stop.test.cjs` continue to pass: `npx vitest run` exits 0.\\n5. `npx biome check scripts/hallucination-audit-stop.cjs tests/hallucination-audit-stop.test.cjs` exits 0 (no new lint/format violations).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `/root/.claude/plugins/cache/jamie-bitflight-skills/hallucination-detector/1.12.4/scripts/hallucination-audit-stop.cjs` |\\n| Test file | `/root/.claude/plugins/cache/jamie-bitflight-skills/hallucination-detector/1.12.4/tests/hallucination-audit-stop.test.cjs` |\\n| Plugin repo | `bitflight-devops/hallucination-detector` (GitHub) |\\n| Prior grooming | `/root/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/jamie-bitflight-skills/.claude/archive/grooming-reports-2026-02-23/grooming-2026-02-21.md` lines 59-81 |\\n| Agent | @javascript-pro (JS fix + matchAll patterns) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: None\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 2 targeted logic changes in one file (if bugs are not already fixed), plus 3 new test cases. If bugs are already fixed, effort is test-only: add 3 test cases covering the two specific scenarios. Estimated 1-2 hours.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Plugin is an external GitHub repo (`bitflight-devops/hallucination-detector`), not in this working directory. Changes must be made there and a new version released for the marketplace cache to update.\\n- The cached version (v1.12.4) appears to have Bug 1 already fixed (BACKTICK_RE and rawText path present at lines 136-186). Verify against the GitHub repo HEAD before implementing \u2014 the fix may already be fully landed.\\n- No regression tests for the specific `rawText` code path or multi-occurrence `because` with mixed evidence. These must be added regardless of bug fix status.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- Source file: `/root/.claude/plugins/cache/jamie-bitflight-skills/hallucination-detector/1.12.4/scripts/hallucination-audit-stop.cjs`\\n- Bug 1 fix present at lines 136-186: `BACKTICK_RE` defined at line 150, `hasEvidenceNearby()` accepts `rawText` parameter at line 173, rawText window check at lines 179-183. Comment at lines 136-140 explicitly documents the fix intent.\\n- Bug 2 behavior at lines 843-878: the `because` branch uses `continue` (line 871) to scan all occurrences. The hedged-because sub-branch uses `break` (line 866) after first match, documented as intentional.\\n- Test file: `/root/.claude/plugins/cache/jamie-bitflight-skills/hallucination-detector/1.12.4/tests/hallucination-audit-stop.test.cjs`\\n- Existing test at line 222 covers `because` suppression via backtick evidence, but uses a string like `'The test fails because \\\\`error code 127\\\\` was returned'` \u2014 this exercises the fix only indirectly. No dedicated `rawText` path test exists.\\n- No test exists for multi-occurrence `because` with mixed evidence/no-evidence positions.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nBug 1 \u2014 Dead backtick evidence marker (verify fix is in place or regressed):\\n1. Call `findTriggerMatches()` with a string containing `because` and nearby inline code: `'The test fails because \\\\`exit code 127\\\\` was returned.'`\\n2. Observe whether `causality_language` match is returned.\\n3. Expected (fixed): no match \u2014 inline code suppresses the flag.\\n4. Broken behavior: match returned \u2014 backtick regex `BACKTICK_RE` was tested on stripped haystack (which has no backticks), so suppression never fired.\\n\\nBug 2 \u2014 Multi-occurrence `because` (verify all non-suppressed occurrences are flagged):\\n1. Call `findTriggerMatches()` with a string containing two `because` occurrences: one with nearby evidence, one without \u2014 e.g. `'It failed because \\\\`exit code 1\\\\` was returned. Also because the config is wrong.'`\\n2. Observe how many `causality_language` matches are returned.\\n3. Expected (fixed): exactly 1 match \u2014 the second occurrence (no evidence) is flagged; the first is suppressed.\\n4. Broken behavior (pre-fix): 0 matches \u2014 `break` after first occurrence caused the loop to exit before reaching the unflagged second occurrence.\\n\",\"digest\":\"29ce00f16f3ba6d285154e10ae479251e70d7cf02aab5149c847623326f34cd5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg5h7A\"}"}